Subject: [PATCH] sycl: kernels for the ternary weight types TQ1_0, TQ2_0 and PTQ1_0

Local gap fill. The SYCL backend had no kernel for TQ1_0 / TQ2_0 (fork patch 0017 gates them out of
supports_op) or PTQ1_0 (carried PR 29672 adds the type, PR 31460's whitelist leaves it out), so
ternary models ran their matmuls on the CPU. CUDA PR 29676 has PTQ1_0 only; TQ1_0 and TQ2_0 have no
GPU port in tree, so all three follow the CPU codec.

- Dequantize (f16, f32, non-contiguous f16) and GET_ROWS through per-weight pair functions:
  dequantize_block_sycl / get_rows_sycl with qr = 1. Prompt batches then use the GEMM route.
- MMVQ, 1..8 columns, and the fused MoE MMVQ: one call covers the 32 weights of one q8_1 block,
  expanded to signed bytes for dp4a. Base-3 digit n of a packed byte is read as the CPU does
  (multiply by 3^n mod 256, then (q * 3) >> 8), four bytes at a time in 16-bit lanes. TQ1_0's
  dot selects its source bytes and digit per step instead of branching per q8_1 block: the branchy
  form passed one column and miscompiled in the multi-column kernel on the CPU OpenCL device.
- 0017's central gate admits these types only as the weight operand of MUL_MAT, MUL_MAT_ID and
  GET_ROWS. SET_ROWS, CPY, DUP / CONT and the other ops still fall back to the CPU; DUP and CONT
  check no types at all, and PTQ1_0 is now caught by the same gate.

